# =============================================================================
# COMPREHENSIVE .DOCKERIGNORE FOR NODE.JS TUTORIAL PROJECT
# Docker build context optimization for Node.js v22.x LTS with Express.js v5.1.0,
# PM2 cluster deployment, comprehensive testing suite, and Flask cross-platform migration
# =============================================================================
#
# Purpose: Optimize Docker build performance, reduce image size, and enhance security
# by excluding unnecessary files and directories from the Docker build context.
#
# Features:
# - Build context size reduction for faster Docker builds and deployments
# - Security-hardened exclusions preventing sensitive files from entering containers
# - Development artifact exclusion maintaining clean production images
# - Cross-platform compatibility supporting Windows, macOS, and Linux development
# - Educational value demonstrating Docker best practices and container security
# - PM2 cluster mode optimization with appropriate file exclusions
# - Multi-stage build support coordinating with Dockerfile COPY instructions
#
# Educational Value:
# - Demonstrates comprehensive Docker ignore patterns for Node.js applications
# - Showcases container security through selective file inclusion strategies
# - Illustrates build performance optimization techniques for production deployment
# - Provides cross-platform development environment compatibility patterns
# - Shows coordination between .gitignore and .dockerignore for different purposes
#
# Version: 1.0.0
# Node.js: v22.x LTS (Production deployment with PM2 cluster mode)
# Express.js: v5.1.0 (Enhanced security and modern JavaScript support)
# Docker: Multi-stage build optimization with security hardening
# PM2: v6.0.8 (Production process management with built-in load balancer)
#
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE.JS DEPENDENCIES AND PACKAGE MANAGEMENT
# Exclude npm/yarn cache and lock files to optimize build context and caching
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Node.js module directories - largest contributor to build context size
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# Package manager cache and configuration
.npm
.yarn-integrity
.yarn/
.pnp.*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Lock files - managed by Dockerfile npm ci command
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# npm configuration and credentials
.npmrc
.npmrc_local
npm-shrinkwrap.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEVELOPMENT TOOLS AND IDE CONFIGURATION
# Exclude development environment files that aren't needed in containers
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Visual Studio Code configuration
.vscode/
.vscode-test/

# IntelliJ IDEA and WebStorm configuration
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# Editor and development tool artifacts
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.settings/
nbproject/
.classpath

# ESLint and Prettier cache files
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
.prettiercache

# Development configuration
nodemon.json
.node-dev.json

