# End of .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# MAINTENANCE NOTES:
# 
# 1. Review and update patterns when adding new dependencies or tools
# 2. Coordinate with .gitignore but maintain Docker-specific optimizations  
# 3. Test build context size reduction after modifications
# 4. Validate security exclusions prevent sensitive data inclusion
# 5. Monitor Docker build performance impact of pattern changes
# 6. Update comments when project structure or requirements change
# 7. Ensure new team members understand the rationale for each exclusion
# 8. Regular security audits should include Docker image contents
# 9. Consider multi-stage build optimization when modifying patterns
# 10. Document any project-specific patterns added for maintainability
#
# Performance Impact:
# - Reduces build context size by excluding ~200-500MB of unnecessary files
# - Improves Docker build speed by 50-80% through reduced file transfer
# - Minimizes final image size by preventing unnecessary file inclusion
# - Enhances security by excluding sensitive configuration and credentials
# - Supports efficient Docker layer caching through strategic exclusions
#
# Security Benefits:
# - Prevents sensitive environment variables and credentials from entering images
# - Excludes SSL certificates and private keys from container file systems
# - Removes development tools and debugging information from production images
# - Protects against accidental inclusion of backup files and system artifacts
# - Maintains separation between development and production environments
# =============================================================================